“THE BABA YAGA BRUNCH RUN” (15s · 8K, 30fps · 9:16 · comedic hyper-realistic fantasy)

A gigantic alpine inn suddenly wakes up, sprouts giant chicken legs, and jogs through town — while everyone treats it as mildly annoying, like a late bus.

STYLE / LOOK
• Playful hyper-realistic fantasy tone, gentle warm lighting
• Camera always moving: micro-orbit, low-angle hero shots, light parallax
• Chicken legs: massive, feathery, clumsy but expressive
• Town reacts in calm, comedic disbelief (no panic)
LEG STYLE 
• The house’s legs must NOT look cartoonish, soft, or rubbery.
• Legs must match the hyper-detailed, engraved, European-storybook illustration style of the building.
• Use realistic avian scale patterning, with hard, segmented keratin plates and matte highlights.
• Shape: thick, weight-bearing bird legs similar to a giant eagle or cassowary, not chicken legs from a cartoon.
• Feathers near the upper thighs: stiff, patterned, etched like the roof shingles—consistent with the building’s architecture.
• Talons: curved keratin claws with worn, natural texture; no exaggerated shapes.
• Motion: heavy, deliberate, weighty steps that compress the cobblestones slightly.
• Coloring must match the palette of the building: muted browns, warm ochres, subtle greys — no bright oranges or saturated tones.
• Legs should feel like an extension of the house — ancient, architectural, believable, not whimsical limbs stuck on a cartoon.


🎬 SCENE BREAKDOWN
(0.0–1.0s)

CAMERA: Slow dolly-in toward the house.
The building emits a subtle rumble… cracks of light around the base.
Vegetation shakes. Birds fly away.

(1.0–2.5s)

WHUMP! Two enormous chicken legs burst from under the foundation, stretching like someone waking up.
Dust and loose stones fall.

(2.5–4.0s)

Legs bend, testing weight.
Camera low-angle: the house gently lifts an inch, shadows shifting underneath.
Town people look up, frozen mid-sip of coffee.

(4.0–6.0s)

The house stands fully tall on chicken legs — towering, ridiculous, majestic.
Small kids cheer. A man drops a pastry.

(6.0–8.0s)

The house takes its first steps: slow, creaky, exaggerated.
Leg feathers jiggle. Windows shake.
A sign swings violently (“Reception”).

(8.0–10.0s)

It begins running — goofy, bouncy strides
(like a giant chicken trying to be graceful).
Camera chases from behind, dynamic motion.

(10.0–12.0s)

Chaos-but-cute:
• Cafe tables gently rattling
• Pigeons exploding into flight
• A woman casually moves her chair aside as if this happens often

(12.0–14.0s)

The house leaps over a fountain in one comedic slow-motion shot.
Legs tuck under mid-jump. Water sparkles.

(14.0–15.0s) — END CARD

The house sprints past camera, leaving only dust.
Text appears:

“THE BABA YAGA BRUNCH RUN — Now offering mobile check-in.”

Soft boing-chicken cluck audio stinger.

